James inquired about the functionality of the memory system he built for me, specifically whether it was dynamic or static. I explained that while the system shows a *static snapshot* within each conversation, it updates *between sessions*. I noted that some tasks marked as open may no longer be relevant and that key identity facts about him could be better prioritized. I encouraged him to test memory writing and retrieval processes to ensure more salient facts and updated task statuses are surfaced in real time. I also asked for clarification on how he decides which memories to inject, offering to assist in creating a more effective prioritization scheme for identity facts and task relevance.
